# Shader sources are byte-input to the compiler: pin LF in the repo AND in the
# working tree so the same fixture feeds identical bytes on every OS (the
# byte-identity tests normalize EOLs defensively, but the checkout should not
# vary in the first place). Verified before adding (git ls-files --eol): every
# tracked *.fx / *.fxh / *.slang is already index-LF, so this renormalizes nothing
# (*.slang added for issue #258; the Slang cross-host byte-identity manifests hash
# the compiled output of these files).
*.fx    text eol=lf
*.fxh   text eol=lf
*.slang text eol=lf

# Compiled shader containers and WASM modules are binary — never EOL-converted,
# never diffed as text. (Already auto-detected as binary today; pinned so a
# future text-looking blob can't be silently mangled.)
*.mgfx binary
*.fxb  binary
*.wasm binary
*.sksl text eol=lf

# Scripts bash (or a shebang) runs: LF in the working tree on every OS, or bash on a Windows
# checkout rejects 'set -euo pipefail' (issue #357). *.py: the validation compare/decode
# scripts carry '#!/usr/bin/env python3', which a CRLF line breaks the same way. Every tracked
# file of these types was already index-LF, so adding the rules renormalized nothing.
# ScriptLineEndingTests pins the checkout.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
